      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PENNY BLACK NZ (9) broke gear and galloped last time but had put together a string of placings prior. Tactics will be crucial from this wide draw but she has the talent to take care of this field. STELLAR EDITION (1) worked to find the lead from a wider barrier and kept kicking to get home by 3.4 metres at this circuit and distance last start, making it four consecutive wins since a spell. The ace draw gives her the chance to extend the winning streak. REINETTE (10) was held up for a clear run last time but was runner-up here when fresh and owns a decent third-up record. Draws to trail the top pick so could be dangerous. BEETASTIC NZ (3) drew on the back row and was held up last time but had recorded two wins and a placing from her previous three. Can bounce back from a better draw.",
